{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787201891078214001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"regardable-superduper-whiteeye","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"96d3d2b77740cd6d98aaf8a2fb387b3fcc3d0f79598a017a16104bad2d80b2f1","event_uuid":"7f4b9ee7-1c9b-4354-9cbd-efbcc34e456d","position":{"commit_sha":"39f7c2fab2e9c95f2e2fe0f993b18d09df50a2d8","position":"1787198160874259001-7f4b9ee7-1c9b-4354-9cbd-efbcc34e456d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fb27c85ba8094783399817661935b5661ccfe72736a648d88fed42858a5d0469","event_uuid":"284e90e5-4c9a-4c45-b7fd-ff841a266c5c","position":{"commit_sha":"7adbb52ef1b77858752a5105dd2cbc52bccb43c7","position":"1787198181944847001-284e90e5-4c9a-4c45-b7fd-ff841a266c5c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787198160874259001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"284e90e5-4c9a-4c45-b7fd-ff841a266c5c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b0a5-f5c0-e516-4fdc"}],"description":"Cost Gerrit change 1942 (ticket silken-stealthful-narwhal) a spurious Verified -1: 1 failed, 14508 passed. The failure is unrelated to that change, which touches only scripts/gen_config_reference.py and tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nTEST: tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated\n\nFAILURE (run 32327846364, job 96302879852, ubuntu py3.13, xdist worker gw3):\n\n  shutil.Error: [('.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                  '.../destination/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                  \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock'\")]\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe test pushes into the bare `source/origin.git` (line ~284, `git push -q origin HEAD:tickets`), which lets git kick off background auto-maintenance in that bare repo. Auto-maintenance takes a plain `$GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY/maintenance.lock` (gc.c, no pid/hostname/staleness — see ticket icicled-unstable-urial for the citation). The very next statement is `shutil.copytree(source_origin, destination_origin, symlinks=True)` (line ~295). copytree scandirs `objects/`, sees `maintenance.lock`, and by the time copy2 opens it the maintenance process has released and unlinked it, so copytree raises.\n\nThis is the SAME root-cause class already fixed for a different test in ticket chewed-illicit-blacklemur (bridge fsck keyset test, stray .git/objects/maintenance.lock on macOS). That fix did not generalise to this test.\n\n## Scope\n\n- tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the copy immune to transient auto-maintenance artifacts rather than retrying: disable auto-maintenance for the repos the test creates (e.g. `git config maintenance.auto false` / `gc.auto 0` on `source_origin` before the push), and/or copy with an ignore predicate that skips `*.lock` under `objects/`. Prefer the config route: it removes the race instead of tolerating it. Then confirm the copy's isolation assertions still hold.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reproduce deterministically by injecting a `maintenance.lock` into `source_origin/objects/` that is unlinked mid-walk, and assert the test still passes.\n- Re-run tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py repeatedly (>=20 iterations) with auto-maintenance enabled and observe zero failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The transient `objects/*.lock` race can no longer fail the copy; checked by a deterministic reproduction that fails before the fix and passes after.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py -q` is green; checked by that command.\n- [ ] The fix removes the race rather than retrying it; checked by review of the diff for absence of retry/sleep loops.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"dca1-f641-caeb-4df4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky: test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin races git auto-maintenance's objects/maintenance.lock","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7f4b9ee7-1c9b-4354-9cbd-efbcc34e456d","284e90e5-4c9a-4c45-b7fd-ff841a266c5c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787201891078214001,"uuid":"0e43c402-7c18-4395-b4e0-ff23540b201a"}